  "body": "## What happens\n\nA generated five-axis program passes generation and verification, but the Fanuc post refuses its first tilted feed.\nI found this while building the catalog case for #2870 on upstream/main d911f455.\n\nThe machine is `assets/machines/tilthead.mch`.\nThe tool is `BN-0600`, with a 60 mm flute and a 6 mm shank diameter.\nThe source is an original closed cylinder along X. Its radius is 12 mm. Its length is 48 mm.\nThe case generates Swarf, 5-Axis Contour, and 5-Axis Flow.\n\nAll three operations generate. `cam.verify()` passes. `cam.post()` refuses the program:\n\n```text\npost blocked - 1 warning(s): a feed that turns A from an angle the post does not know - the stated A rate cannot be held\n```\n\n## Cause\n\n`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/stamp.rs:173-215` leaves the opening rapid moves without a pose.\nThe first tilted feed introduces the rotary angles.\n`assets/posts/fanuc.cps` starts with unknown rotary angles.\n`crates/post/src/post/rotary_cap.rs:95-108` correctly refuses a feed from an unknown angle when the machine states a rotary rate.\n\nThe generator and the post disagree about the initial rotary state.\nThis report does not ask to remove the rate guard.\n\n## Done means\n\nA generated five-axis path establishes its rotary state before the first tilted feed, or gives a specific generation refusal.\nTests cover the opening moves and posting with the tilt-head machine.\nThe direct feed-first stream still refuses an unknown initial angle.\nThe catalog script for #2870 posts without a guard bypass or an unrelated positioning operation.\n\neffort:high - The fix changes generated or posted tool motion. The safety floor applies.\n\nFound while working #2870. Catalog umbrella: #2392.\n",
